      "writtenOn": "2018-10-03T15:56:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If reset is not required - there is no point in starting this timer, as the only thing which factory_enable_failed() does is deasserting the reset, which would not be asserted if reset_required_ is false.\n\nThis all is a bit of a mess, what happens is that the ccd_config_changed() callback above runs before line 91 is executed, but I am not sure if this is guaranteed.\n\nnote that factory_enable_failed() is also called in line 92, so that function before deasserting the reset should check if it was asserted.",
      "parentUuid": "467480a0_3b706e14",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 94,
        "startChar": 0,
